{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1442294-adventure-how-did-the-adventure-era-really-ended","id":1442294,"title":"[Adventure!] How did the adventure era really ended?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-01T13:02:06-07:00","id":1442294,"title":"[Adventure!] How did the adventure era really ended?","content":"Hello Everyone,<br /> <br /> While my topic about the influence of the inspired in the world is all about speculating how the timeline would diverge, this topic is about speculating how the inspired, and their actions, disappeared by the end of World War 2 according to &quot;official&quot; canon (we still need to see the appendix section of adventure). So, what really happened? What follows is just my personal theory, feel free to share yours.<br /> <br /> The most common explanation is that the telluric energies of the hammersmith incident faded away to nothing by the end of the 40s and with that the inspired. Although this no doubt played a role, the question remains about the actions and inventions of the inspired. How could they just disappear? Where there no records kept? Did the whole world just decide that none of it was real? Again, something similar to project rewrite could have happened where the governments of the world decided to erase any trace of the inspired. Why did they do it? Well, for the same reason as someone else did it.<br /> <br /> You see, for me the one who really ended the adventure era was none other than Max Mercer.<br /> <br /> Let's keep in mind that Max is no ordinary Daredevil, he's a time traveler. In one of his jumps he travelled to a future where the inspired were more numerous and active in world affairs, including the second world war. Now imagine hundreds, if not thousands, of inspired in the most devastating conflict humanity ever saw. Max didn't need to imagine it because he saw it, hell he even saw the end of it... and let's just say it wasn't pretty.<br /> <br /> Max was left with no other choice, there was only one way to stop it. He had to destroy any source of telluric energy in the world, and so he did in secret for years, without anyone knowing...sadly even a time traveler has blind spots, especially when it comes to friends.<br /> <br /> Feeling isolated and with many doubts as the years went by, Max finally confessed to Primoris and Bhurano. Bhurano, although upset, decided to forgive Max and trust his judgement. Primoris...well, we all know how it ended don't we? This is what caused the final breach between Max and Primoris, which lead to what I call the third front.<br /> <br /> Even thought Max actions did stop the terrible future he witnessed, he didn't completely eradicate it. While humanity was busy fighting, the Aeon society and other allegiances fought a secret war against the inspired that worked with Primoris (who worked with the Axis to use their resources), till Primoris was finally defeated. Very few records mention this secret front, which has become but another of many myths and stories from the great war.<br /> <br /> So there you have it, feel free to share your opinion and speculations. I'm curious to see what you all have imagined.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T14:23:14-07:00","id":1442318,"title":"","content":"Personally, I go with a more &quot;heat death of the universe&quot; approach. Rather than having the Flux energy disappear, when the Hammersmith Event occurred, a number of places and peoples were focused in on, making them anomalies or Talents or what-have-you. Flux is the most mobile of the three, and the most predominant with the Hammersmith event. As time passed, the flux energy dispersed and spread out, eventually spreading too thin to provide any real benefit to people, causing Talents to lose their powers and Strange Places to lose their other-ness. As for Mesmerists and Stalwarts, well, they just didn't have enough Noetic or Quantum Energy built up in their bodies to retain their abilities, so even though those powers aren't as free-flowing as Flux, they still escaped all the same. The Telluric energy didn't altogether disappear, it's just been rendered impotent at this stage, and any mini-Events which occur until Aberrant only gather enough Telluric energy to do something rather than generate more of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T14:26:03-07:00","id":1442319,"title":"","content":"Given that Max Mercer started the aeon Society specifically to inspire people and to uncover the mysteries associated with tularoic energy, I find it very much out of character for him to turn around and start suppressing it.<br /> <br /> I mean, even if you did see the sort of future that you described, I don't see him deciding that the inspired age needs to be destroyed. Rather, I picture him deciding that that future needs to be overcome. If anything, he would double down on his effort to inspire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T14:29:56-07:00","id":1442320,"title":"","content":"Also note that it is canon that the Doyen erected a protective shell around Earth in response to the Hammersmith event, and that similar events between then and the galatea event were largely suppressed as a result. It would not surprise me if this turned out to be the factor that caused the end of the adventure age. Or at least a contributing factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T15:26:41-07:00","id":1442323,"title":"","content":"As a Carnivale fan, I like the idea the Trinity blast knocked the dimensions that started overlapping as a result of the Hammersmith Event back out of alignment, resulting in (from a prime timeline pov) the disappearance of all the Martian city states, hollow earth, Atlantean ruins, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T15:34:15-07:00","id":1442324,"title":"","content":"Agree with Dataweaver. Max Mercer is hardly involved in the end of Adventure Era and the Doyen Barrier is probably the one responsible.<br /> <br /> Critian Caceorte has a more abrupt vision of the end than I, but I think he is right in the way it decayed to nothing. I think the number of new Talents, Stalwarts and Mesmerists fall to the more \u201cnormal\u201d level over the years, and the old ones retired and died over the years, not losing their powers, but keeping it and slowly hiding it to avoid other people to try to study them or just to have a normal life with their families.<br /> <br /> The largest strange places start to fading away, letting some strange artifacts or minor strange places. You may not find the sapient gorilla city in Congo, but maybe you find some artifacts built by them, or even a part of the ancient city as a weird part of a cavern, or the last of their kind lost and aging as a relic of what once was a entire civilization.<br /> <br /> I would keep the weird places around, I think people just stop caring and left they alone. Worse than that, they were not explored by that many people, what happened is that it were a more adventurous aspect, and when the explorers left and the scientists come it was not fun anymore to be published, and you have the History Channel shows about strange places as discredited as the shows about aliens in the history.<br /> <br /> it\u2019s possible that Aeon society Babel Dossier or another allegiance start working as the Sanctuary, from the Sanctuary, or as SCP Fundation. Just hiding everything they can and avoiding people to run into places they should not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 04-01-2021, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T22:50:40-07:00","id":1442363,"title":"","content":"Now I want to run a <b>Trinity</b> game with various eras in it, where PCs are from, for example, <b>Modern TC</b>, start to uncover Lost City - and then action takes back to 1930's where their grandparents uncovered this place in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Add to me some <b>Aeon</b> era hack to that location - and we have multi timeline truly <i><b>Continuum</b></i> game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T04:06:27-07:00","id":1442384,"title":"","content":"I have thought of doing something akin to that. Except I would start in AEon. That way I can flashback to &quot;X&quot; era to reveal something they need to know to deal with the issue in AEon.<br /> <br /> OR....play characters in Adventure! and then let the player's choices actually affect the timeline. What they do causes the Aberrant era. And their actions in Aberrant force the AEon era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T05:19:10-07:00","id":1442391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1442294-adventure-how-did-the-adventure-era-really-ended?p=1442319#post1442319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Max Mercer started the aeon Society specifically to inspire people and to uncover the mysteries associated with tularoic energy, I find it very much out of character for him to turn around and start suppressing it.<br /> <br /> I mean, even if you did see the sort of future that you described, I don't see him deciding that the inspired age needs to be destroyed. Rather, I picture him deciding that that future needs to be overcome. If anything, he would double down on his effort to inspire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like a gardener. Roses are profoundly desired, but not in the lilly beds. The inspired are desired, having them destroy civilization and devolve into warlords wasn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T06:08:27-07:00","id":1442395,"title":"","content":"I always figured Max was playing the long game to get humanity past the Aeon age. He knew the Aberrant War needed to happen, and probably knows about the threats of the time. Once/If Humanity can get past those, they can walk the path to transcendence the Doyen tried to leapfrog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T01:28:12-07:00","id":1443571,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Telluric energy&quot; (quantum flux) fades almost back to pre-Hammersmith event levels, sealing away the connections to &quot;Strange Places&quot; (other universes/timelines) and greatly reducing the number of new Inspired. Stalwarts and Mesmercists find their abilities shifting into Nova's (possibly) and Psiads (definitely) as the amount of &quot;Telluric energy&quot; decreases.<br /> <br /> While this is not nessicarily enough to end the era on it's own, I do feel it does pkay a substantial role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T02:22:52-07:00","id":1443574,"title":"","content":"Telluric Energy is not only Quantum, but also Noetic energy and Flux. Any of the 3 is considered Telluric, including any mix of the 3, like the one relieved in the Hammersmith incident.<br /> <br /> It was suggested that Stalwarts are Novas of low quantum, and Mesmerists are Psiads of low Psi, and the way Inspiration works is more a system mechanic than a in world mechanic. Basically, if a Stalwart train enough they will eventually reach Q2 or more, and you (as player) would need to change systems to be capable of describing their powers, but from his point of view it\u2019s only an evolution.<br /> <br /> Until we have a proper read in the Gifts session, we can\u2019t guess where is the Nova going to start when they finish the Adventure campaign, or what means in psi terms having a certain Inspiration, but I think once we have enough information we will be able to pick an stalwart sheet and translate it into a nova sheet easily, and the same for Mesmerists into Psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T05:42:03-07:00","id":1443581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1442294-adventure-how-did-the-adventure-era-really-ended?p=1443571#post1443571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Telluric energy&quot; (quantum flux) fades almost back to pre-Hammersmith event levels, sealing away the connections to &quot;Strange Places&quot; (other universes/timelines) and greatly reducing the number of new Inspired. Stalwarts and Mesmercists find their abilities shifting into Nova's (possibly) and Psiads (definitely) as the amount of &quot;Telluric energy&quot; decreases.<br /> <br /> While this is not nessicarily enough to end the era on it's own, I do feel it does pkay a substantial role.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMHO, the shift from stalwart to nova and mesmerist to psiad, if it happens at all, isn't the result of a <i>drop</i> in Telluric Energies, but of a <i>resurgence</i> of them. For example, the Galatea event. <br /> <br /> I say \u201cif it happens at all\u201d because stalwarts and mesmerists are types of Inspired: like Talents, they have Inspiration and Facets; like Talents (and explicitly unlike novas and psiads), they have access to Dramatic Editing, which in the Trinity Continuum is explicitly about manipulating Flux. They differ from Talents only in terms of what Gifts they have available to them. <br /> <br /> In short, it might be better to think of them being to novas and psiads as quantakinetics are to aberrants: broadly speaking, daredevils, stalwarts, and mesmerists are all essentially the same thing, manipulators of Flux; but the latter two use their ability to manipulate Flux to indirectly manipulate Quantum and Psi, respectively. <br /> <br /> I could see the possibility that as the Telluric Energies from the Hammersmith Event subside, the stalwarts and mesmerists lose access to those energies and have nothing to manipulate; and their Gifts effectively go dormant until a resurgence of the appropriate type of energies. They still retain their ability to engage in Dramatic Editing; so they don't <i>quite</i> go back to being baselines. But, for instance, a stalwart or mesmerist in the core book's setting would mostly look like a Talent who lacks Gifts. Without ambient Quantum or Noetic energies to manipulate, they'd come across as inferior to those Talents whose Gifts <i>don't</i> hinge on ambient energies to function. <br /> <br /> This would mean that you could incorporate stalwarts and mesmerists into TC:Ab and TC:\u00c6 if you wish. In both subsequent eras, the mesmerists would probably be mistaken for psiads; in TC:Ab, stalwarts would tend to be mistaken for \u201cdark stars\u201d/\u201cstealth novas\u201d, while in TC:\u00c6, they'd be mistaken for Superiors. But they wouldn't <i>quite</i> be the same thing: as mentioned above, the single biggest difference would be that they'd retain their access to Dramatic Editing. <br /> <br /> That said, I'd probably also allow them to transition: as a subconscious choice, an existing mesmerist encountering the flood of energies released by the Galatea Event might subconsciously choose to attune herself fully to the Noetic energies, replacing her Inspiration with a boost in Psi and trading out her Gifts for Aptitudes; or an existing stalwart might choose to Erupt as a nova, replacing his Inspiration with Quantum and his Gifts with Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges, and Quantum Powers. Doing so would cost them their access to Dramatic Editing, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-12-2021, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T06:14:13-07:00","id":1443584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1442294-adventure-how-did-the-adventure-era-really-ended?p=1443581#post1443581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, the shift from stalwart to nova and mesmerist to psiad, if it happens at all, isn't the result of a <i>drop</i> in Telluric Energies, but of a <i>resurgence</i> of them. For example, the Galatea event.<br /> <br /> This would mean that you could incorporate stalwarts and mesmerists into TC:Ab and TC:\u00c6 if you wish. In both subsequent eras, the mesmerists would probably be mistaken for psiads; in TC:Ab, stalwarts would tend to be mistaken for \u201cdark stars\u201d/\u201cstealth novas\u201d, while in TC:\u00c6, they'd be mistaken for Superiors. But they wouldn't <i>quite</i> be the same thing: as mentioned above, the single biggest difference would be that they'd retain their access to Dramatic Editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this angle. From the Adventure material presented so-far, Stalwarts already look to have the superbeing power level that I prefer in a game, and in comics.<br /> <br /> For my druthers, I would say that any transition between &quot;eras&quot; would be a result of the Doyen barrier, and subsequent attempts to punch through it. As Flux is both Quantum and Subquantum energy, an imperfect attempt to punch through the barrier might only let one type of energy to come through, creating an imbalance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-12-2021, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T06:26:43-07:00","id":1443590,"title":"","content":"Ian said Dramatic Editing works different for Stalwarts and Mesmerists, tomorrow we may have a better idea, but I think it\u2019s more related to extending their powers beyond the gifts they already have and less with bending reality as Talents do.<br /> <br /> Also Ian said Stalwarts and Mesmerists are Novas and Psiads, so I don\u2019t think they are really different, just described different by the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T09:45:35-07:00","id":1443606,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to seeing with what they come up with. That said, I'm a little leery with calling something \u201cDramatic Editing\u201d if it doesn't involve altering or adding elements to the narrative. I'm perfectly fine with stalwarts and mesmerists having alternatives to the daredevils' Dramatic Editing; in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1428557-tc-adventure-%E2%80%94-prototype-edition\">TC: Adventure! Prototype edition</a> hack, I even proposed a couple, such as stalwarts getting a \u201cPlus Ultra\u201d ability, to borrow a term from My Hero Academia, or mesmerists getting an Attunement ability; but neither of those strike me as being suited to be called \u201cDramatic Editing\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T12:39:06-07:00","id":1443629,"title":"","content":"Ok, to get back on track to my topic, it seems that I haven't explained myself well enough and for that I apologize. This topic is all about speculation and personal interpretations, I'm not looking for definitive answers. I'm just curious about your perspectives till we get a look at the last chapter.<br /> <br /> Let me clarify, I already know about the barrier that the Doyen put and the official explanation, what I wanted to know is how (almost) every single trace of the adventure era was erased. Does the disappearance of telluric energy also erased everyone's memory? Destroyed every inspired device? Rewrote every action of the inspired? And the consequences of their actions? Hell, what happened to the talking gorillas? The answer could be yes to all, maybe as telluric energy fades it also erases or diminishes everything that touches, it's one explanation. Maybe the effect wasn't so strong, but then it was combined with many of the alliances working together to erase any proof of the adventure era. <br /> <br /> The scenario I described with Max Mercer ending the adventure era was simply my way to make sense of it. The decline of telluric energy and a global conspiracy weren't enough (in my mind). So who better to erase all traces of a timeline than a time traveler? This doesn't make Max a villain, I still believe he is the idealist hero trying to make the world a better place. He just saw what the raw power of inspiration could do if unchecked and tried to reign it in, not destroy it completely. But we all know that good intentions don't always end in good actions, do we?<br /> <br /> I hope my intention is more clear now. Thanks in advance for your answers. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T12:56:16-07:00","id":1443632,"title":"","content":"Without being too tangental, one could run it as if it hasn't ended. I find the Adventure! world too interesting to allow it to fade into nothing, so to speak. Along those lines, I have been pondering running the different eras of the Trinity Continuum as if they were actually happening in parallel in alternate timelines (with timey wimey effect to allow them to be occurring at the same time).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T13:06:09-07:00","id":1443634,"title":"","content":"This is a really cool thread. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a. I agree that mesmerists, stalwarts and daredevils are essentially just era-specific variants of psiad, nova and Talent respectively and not entirely new types of Inspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T13:08:53-07:00","id":1443635,"title":"","content":"Why are you insisting that all traces of it be removed? Personally, I prefer that it had lasting impact. Sure, some of the more bizarre strange places can end up disappearing. And much of the more bizarre technology will be powered super science, which means that it will fail as soon as the telluric energy levels drop enough. Inspired technology and advanced technology are both more likely to stick around, but the inspired technology will be in effect One of a kind prototypes; not the sort of thing that's going to revolutionize the industrial base. Advanced technology does have the potential to revolutionize the industrial base; but it is unlikely to be all that fantastic. It tends to be improved versions of what technology is already present. That can definitely lead to changes in the long run, such as more fuel efficient and or less polluting cars. And as I may have said earlier in this thread, it is now part of my head-canon that the adventure era ended up sewing the seeds that will eventually develop into the aeon era's africa.<br /> <br /> As for Max Mercer, my issue with your proposed scenario isn't that it makes him villainous. I have no problem with the notion of the well-intentioned extremist. The problem I have with your take on Max Mercer is that it runs completely counter to his personality. The only thing that's consistent between your max Mercer and the published Max Mercer is that they are both time travelers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T13:10:14-07:00","id":1443637,"title":"","content":"So here is my perspective on things.<br /> <br /> In my view, in the canon timeline that leads from Adventure! to Aberrant to Aeon the Inspired age of the first game begins with a bang and ends with a slow whimper as the energy from the starting event, the Hammersmith Incident, fades. Those who were Inspired never (ever ever ever times infinity) loose their abilities, nor their potential for growth, it just sees less and less new ones forming. That said less and less does not ever (ever ever ever) reach zero, meaning there will always be a few that become Inspired. With most of them being Talents (Daredevils), though also some Mesmerists and Stalwarts too.<br /> <br /> Its the same with Novas and Psiads, the potential for a human to become one always exists and so maybe one in ten million humans may naturally become either of those type, even in periods where the energy is low.<br /> <br /> This all said, I do not look at Adventure! as having its end written, nor Aberrant, nor Aeon. To me, the future of the game line being played is open. So, for me, in my game, the answer of 'when did the Inspired Age fade' is 'it doesn't have to, not unless the players want it to'. Its the same with the question 'how does the Nova Age end,' with my answer being 'in an Aberrant game do not assume that the events leading to the Aberrant War will occur.'<br /> <br /> From a in-universe perspective, for me, the path from Adventure! to Aberrant to Aeon is but one path history may take. In a parallel world the nature of things is such that the Inspired never fade, and so the 60s and 70s and 80s and 90s, and even 2000s, are all the age of the Inspired. In another parallel world instead of the Hammersmith Incident leading to the Inspired it leads to Novas, and in another it leads to Psiads. In another world the Galatea Explosion hid the rise of Psiads, rather than Novas. In another, the fall of Psions in the 2100s lead to the rise of Novas.<br /> <br /> What I am saying is that the greater universe that exists leads to there being the great potential for the Inspired never fading, never going away.<br /> <br /> That said, there is also something cool about cycles. That until humanity is ready for all three to be equal periods of no dominance fade to periods where one of the three dominate. Maybe the Inspired age, where a version of all three energies are equally dominant, serves as a stepping stone to what may be our potential future.<br /> <br /> When it comes to how things get hidden I think its less a conspiracy and more a sense of disbelief. While the individual talking gorilla never looses his intelligence in time his kin stay in their place of power to the point nobody else remembers them. And when someone talks about them people around them think it was something from an old comic. When it comes to Telluric weapons without the inspired to power them the weapon becomes useless, a simple curiosity. As far as golden flying cities, they are weather balloons being tested by the Air Force or some ridiculous plan made by a wartime government that never got off the table.<br /> <br /> That or the Aeon Society actually cleaned up, maybe with the help of allied government agencies. I mean as time goes on and newer generations grow up without seeing the 'magic' of the Inspired then it becomes harder and harder to 'prove' that it every happened. Of course another option is that a normal person saw something an Inspired did or invented and then worked hard to make a mundane version - so the question becomes instead of how to hide the 'magic' its more 'how to make the magic usable by everyone'. The Inspired with the special gun becomes the next generation common weapon, same with vehicles and other technologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 04-12-2021, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T13:37:10-07:00","id":1443644,"title":"","content":"I would amend that only with the observation that most of the inspired do not have inherently lengthened lifespans. So if they're in their 30s in the 1930s, then they'll be in their 60s in the 1960s. Unless you're one of the rare few that has longevity, your abilities will have faded to an extent by then. By the '80s, you'll be in your 80s. And so on. The adventure era fades away as the inspired age out (and die off, because adventuring is not a particularly safe occupation). As I mentioned in my last post, I have more of a concern with the effects of the super science that the era introduces; but even that gets mitigated as time goes by, as the stuff that isn't \u201cmerely\u201d advanced either stops working or becomes unique artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T14:59:37-07:00","id":1443653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1442294-adventure-how-did-the-adventure-era-really-ended?p=1443635#post1443635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you insisting that all traces of it be removed? Personally, I prefer that it had lasting impact. Sure, some of the more bizarre strange places can end up disappearing. And much of the more bizarre technology will be powered super science, which means that it will fail as soon as the telluric energy levels drop enough. Inspired technology and advanced technology are both more likely to stick around, but the inspired technology will be in effect One of a kind prototypes; not the sort of thing that's going to revolutionize the industrial base. Advanced technology does have the potential to revolutionize the industrial base; but it is unlikely to be all that fantastic. It tends to be improved versions of what technology is already present. That can definitely lead to changes in the long run, such as more fuel efficient and or less polluting cars. And as I may have said earlier in this thread, it is now part of my head-canon that the adventure era ended up sewing the seeds that will eventually develop into the aeon era's africa.<br /> <br /> As for Max Mercer, my issue with your proposed scenario isn't that it makes him villainous. I have no problem with the notion of the well-intentioned extremist. The problem I have with your take on Max Mercer is that it runs completely counter to his personality. The only thing that's consistent between your max Mercer and the published Max Mercer is that they are both time travelers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my preferred flavor. That the Inspired world didn't end, but it might become harder to see for the world at large. When it comes to Super Science- Inspired Tech is great for making giant robots, foo fighters and teleportation portals, but not so good at making something to make a normal joe's life any easier. IMO, Super-Science is usually just too weird to be practical or have much lasting effect. Though it can inspire others to try to make a mundane version. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T21:02:01-07:00","id":1443692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1442294-adventure-how-did-the-adventure-era-really-ended?p=1443632#post1443632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find the Adventure! world too interesting to allow it to fade into nothing, so to speak. Along those lines, I have been pondering running the different eras of the Trinity Continuum as if they were actually happening in parallel in alternate timelines (with timey wimey effect to allow them to be occurring at the same time).</div> </div> </div> </div>I joked in other topic that all Adventure! era weirdness move TO THE MOON! by the end of it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What I meant here that Strange Places lose contact with Earth made on Hammersmith Incidents. Those Places and Artifacts a